. do testing3c2.do 

. /*===========================================================================
> ===
>   testing3c2.do
>   Build a synthetic panel that reaches HAD sub-case "none" via the QS-REJECTE
> D
>   route: had_tie = 0 (no mass point) and did_had's quasi-stayer test rejects.
> 
>   Working directory must be Stata/. Read the log; Stata's exit code lies.
> 
>   Target state:
>       design      = HAD
>       n_stayers   = 0          (else -> "stayers")
>       had_tie     = 0          (else -> "none" via the mass-point short-circu
> it,
>                                 which is case 3c-i, not what we want here)
>       qs_pval < 0.05           (else -> "quasi-stayers")
>       had_case    = "none"
> 
>   QS = D(1) / (D(2) - D(1)) over the positive doses at the switch; rejects wh
> en
>   QS > 19, i.e. p = 1/(1+QS) < 0.05. So we need the two smallest positive dos
> es
>   CLOSE TOGETHER relative to the smallest one -- doses bounded away from 0 an
> d
>   densely packed.
> 
>   Reference: had_data1.dta, which does produce a QS test, has 1000 groups,
>   10 periods, doses ~U(0,1) continuous. Small panels (6 groups) fail inside
>   did_had with r(3301) because lprobust cannot fit a local polynomial.
> =============================================================================
> =*/
. 
. clear all

. set more off

. discard

. 
. 
. 
. /*---------------------------------------------------------------------------
> ---
>   ATTEMPT 1 -- 1000 groups, doses U(10, 11), switch at t=6 of 10
>   Mirrors had_data1's shape exactly; only the dose support moves away from 0.
>   With 1000 draws on an interval of width 1, consecutive order statistics are
>   ~0.001 apart while D(1) ~ 10, so QS ~ 10/0.001 = 10000 >> 19.
> -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
> -*/
. 
. di as text _n "{hline 78}"

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

. di as text "ATTEMPT 1 -- 1000 groups, doses U(10,11), switch t=6"
ATTEMPT 1 -- 1000 groups, doses U(10,11), switch t=6

. di as text "{hline 78}"
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

. 
. clear

. set seed 20261006

. set obs 1000
Number of observations (_N) was 0, now 1,000.

. gen g = _n

. gen double dose = 10 + runiform()          // positive, bounded away from 0

. expand 10
(9,000 observations created)

. bys g: gen t = _n

. gen double d = cond(t >= 6, dose, 0)

. gen double y = g/100 + t + rnormal()

. 
. whichDIDshouldIuse y g t d, detail

----------------------------------------------------------------------
  DESIGN: Heterogeneous Adoption Design (HAD)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
  All groups untreated at baseline (t=   1); all 1000 treated
  group(s) experience treatment at t=   6, but the size
  of that change varies across groups.

  Sub-case: no stayers or quasi-stayers -- the lowest dose
  is not close to 0.
    QS =  4.0e+04, p = 0.000  (N = 1000, reject at 5% if QS > 19)
  WARNING: without stayers or quasi-stayers, WATT is not identified
  under parallel trends alone. Using the least-treated as controls
  needs a bounded-heterogeneity assumption (BOUND-HET), which
  pretrends cannot test, and then identifies only the SIGN of WATT.
  Estimator: did_had
  See Chapter 7 of the DID textbook; de Chaisemartin et al. (2026).
----------------------------------------------------------------------

----------------------------------------------------------------------
  whichDIDshouldIuse:  Y=y  G=g  T=t  D=d
  missing treatment: default (less strict)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Panel:   10 periods, calendar    1 ..   10
       (t normalized to 1..  10; never-switcher sentinel =   11)

Groups dropped:
  treatment never observed:              0
  groups retained:                       1000 of 1000

Missing treatment (default rules; use , strict to drop instead):
  late entrants, baseline taken at entry:        0
  d missing at start, baseline taken later:      0
  pre-switch gaps read as baseline:              0
  gap right before switch, demoted to control:   0
  controls leaving the panel early:              0
  switchers with d missing after the switch:     0

----------------------------------------------------------------------
  DIAGNOSTICS
----------------------------------------------------------------------
  n_groups             = 1000
  n_switchers          = 1000
  n_never_treated      = 0   (usable at the earliest switch)
  n_truncated_controls = 0
  never_treated_groups = 0
  any_switchers        = 1
  same_Fg              = 1   (sd(Fg|switchers) = 0)
  switch periods (t)   =  6 ..  6
  switch dates (t_cal) =    6 ..    6
  is_binary            = 0   (d in {0, 10.997866})
  is_binary01          = 0
  is_absorbing         = 0
  zero_baseline        = 1   (groups with d_baseline!=0: 0)
  common_baseline      = 1
  heterog_dose         = 1   (sd(first_change) = .28795528)
  nonneg_dose          = 1   (min dose at the switch = 10.00005)
  n_stayers            = 0
  had_d_min            = 10.00005   (lowest positive dose at the switch)
  had_tie              = 0
  n_at_d_min           = 1   (groups at the lowest dose)
  n_above_d_min        = 999   (groups above it)
  sfsd_pair            = 0   (groups in cells with a usable pair: 0)
  n_baseline_cells     = 1
  n_sfsd_cells         = 0   (cells carrying timing variation)
  n_post_gap_switchers = 0
----------------------------------------------------------------------

. 
. di as text _n "  r(design)    = " as result "`r(design)'"   as text "   want 
> HAD"

  r(design)    = HAD   want HAD

. di as text    "  r(had_case)  = " as result "`r(had_case)'" as text "   want 
> none"
  r(had_case)  = none   want none

. di as text    "  r(had_tie)   = " as result r(had_tie)      as text "   want 
> 0"
  r(had_tie)   = 0   want 0

. di as text    "  r(n_stayers) = " as result r(n_stayers)    as text "   want 
> 0"
  r(n_stayers) = 0   want 0

. di as text    "  r(qs_stat)   = " as result r(qs_stat)      as text "   want 
> > 19"
  r(qs_stat)   = 40175.525   want > 19

. di as text    "  r(qs_pval)   = " as result r(qs_pval)      as text "   want 
> < 0.05"
  r(qs_pval)   = .00002489   want < 0.05

. 
. 
. /*---------------------------------------------------------------------------
> ---
>   ATTEMPT 2 -- same shape, but a MARGINAL rejection
> 
>   Attempt 1 works but is extreme: QS ~ 4.0e+04, printed in scientific notatio
> n
>   by the report's %6.3f. A panel that rejects just past the 5% line is a bett
> er
>   example -- it shows the test deciding rather than being overwhelmed.
> 
>   QS = D(1)/(D(2)-D(1)), so to land near 19 we need the gap between the two
>   smallest doses to be about D(1)/19. Rather than fight the order statistics 
> of
>   a random draw, set the two lowest doses BY HAND and scatter the rest well
>   above them:
>         D(1) = 2.00, D(2) = 2.10  ->  QS = 2.00/0.10 = 20,  p = 1/21 = 0.048
> -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
> -*/
. 
. di as text _n(2) "{hline 78}"


------------------------------------------------------------------------------

. di as text "ATTEMPT 2 -- 1000 groups, two lowest doses pinned for QS ~ 20"
ATTEMPT 2 -- 1000 groups, two lowest doses pinned for QS ~ 20

. di as text "{hline 78}"
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

. 
. clear

. set seed 20261006

. set obs 1000
Number of observations (_N) was 0, now 1,000.

. gen g = _n

. * bulk of the groups sit well above the two lowest doses
. gen double dose = 5 + 5*runiform()

. * pin the two smallest positive doses
. replace dose = 2.00 if g == 1
(1 real change made)

. replace dose = 2.10 if g == 2
(1 real change made)

. expand 10
(9,000 observations created)

. bys g: gen t = _n

. gen double d = cond(t >= 6, dose, 0)

. gen double y = g/100 + t + rnormal()

. 
. whichDIDshouldIuse y g t d, detail

